### String to Integer (atoi)

**Problem:** Given a string, convert it into a 32-bit signed integer. Ignore leading whitespaces, handle the optional sign (`+` or `-`), and convert the valid numeric characters into an integer while handling overflow and underflow.

**Approach:**
- Skip all leading whitespace characters.
- Check for an optional positive (`+`) or negative (`-`) sign.
- Traverse the string and process consecutive numeric digits.
- Convert each character into its corresponding integer digit.
- Build the result by multiplying the current number by 10 and adding the new digit.
- Stop when a non-digit character is encountered.
- Handle integer overflow and underflow by clamping the result within the 32-bit signed integer range.
- Return the final integer with the appropriate sign.

**Time Complexity:** O(n) – We traverse the string at most once.

**Space Complexity:** O(1) – Only a constant amount of extra space is used.

**Concepts Used:**
- String Traversal
- Character Handling
- ASCII Values
- Type Conversion
- Conditional Statements
- Overflow and Underflow Handling

###Solution

class Solution {
    public int myAtoi(String s) {
        int i=0;
        int n=s.length();
        int sign=1;
        long num=0;
        while(i<n && s.charAt(i)==' ')
        {
            i++;
        }
        if(i<n && s.charAt(i)=='-')
        {
            sign=-1;
            i++;
        }
        else if(i<n && s.charAt(i)=='+')
        {
            sign=1;
            i++;
        }
        while(i<n && s.charAt(i)>='0' && s.charAt(i)<='9')
        {
           int digit=s.charAt(i)-'0';
           num = num*10 + digit;
           if(sign==1 && num>Integer.MAX_VALUE) return Integer.MAX_VALUE;
           if(sign== -1 && -num<Integer.MIN_VALUE) return Integer.MIN_VALUE;
           i++;
        }
        return (int)(sign*num);
    }
}
